  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Sunday)\nIssued at 1257 PM CDT MON OCT 19 2026\n\nUpper-level ridging will remain uninterrupted through the middle\nof the week, allowing for afternoon highs to continue climbing\ninto the mid-70s and upper-80s. However, by Wednesday, it still\nappears as if the region will transition into N/NE flow aloft, as\na deep trough takes shape over the East Coast, and ridging builds\nto our west. As a result, temperatures will slightly decrease in\nour east, as cooler air filters down through the Appalachian\nMountain range via a CAD wedge. Overnight lows will remain on the\ncooler side as well through the forecast period, as decoupled\nwinds will allow for light radiational cooling each night.\n\nGiven the lack of deep moisture in the overhead column of air,\nand a lack of proper forcing mechanism, little to no rainfall\nremains expected the next seven days.\n\n/44/",
